Replay Chess analysis worker — third-party notices
=================================================

This image runs third-party software. The worker image is private (GHCR package "replay-chess-analysis-worker",
ghcr.io/replay-chess/replay-chess-analysis-worker, never published; the deploy workflow fails unless GHCR reports it
private): running Stockfish as a service is not distribution (phase-03 plan §11.4, P3-Q9, LIC-3). This file records
what would be needed to comply with the GPL if the image were ever shared.

Stockfish 18
------------
- Upstream: https://github.com/official-stockfish/Stockfish
- Version: tag sf_18, commit cb3d4ee9b47d0c5aae855b12379378ea1439675c (checked by the Dockerfile at build time)
- Build: `make profile-build ARCH=armv8-dotprod COMP=gcc` on debian:bookworm-slim (arm64), stripped
- Networks (embedded in the binary; file names are the first 12 hex digits of their SHA-256):
    big   nn-c288c895ea92.nnue
    small nn-37f18f62d772.nnue
- Licence: GNU General Public License v3.0. The full text, the AUTHORS file and the exact build record
  (net and binary SHA-256 digests) are in the image at /usr/local/share/doc/stockfish/{Copying.txt,AUTHORS,BUILD_INFO}.
- Corresponding source: the upstream tag and commit above, unmodified.
- The worker talks to the engine over UCI (stdin/stdout) as a separate process; no Stockfish code is linked into the
  worker.

Lichess evaluation database
---------------------------
- `lichess_db_eval.jsonl.zst` from https://database.lichess.org/#evals, CC0 1.0 (public domain dedication).
- Used offline only (scripts/seed-evalcache.ts) to seed the eval cache with opening positions; the attribution
  "Opening evaluations from the Lichess open database, CC0" appears on How we grade.

Lichess chess-openings
----------------------
- The opening lines the seed builder replays (apps/web/public/openings/*.tsv) are the Lichess chess-openings dataset,
  CC0 1.0.

npm dependencies
----------------
